---
source: crates/ruff_python_formatter/tests/fixtures.rs
input_file: crates/ruff_python_formatter/resources/test/fixtures/ruff/identity_operators.by
---
## Input
```bython
# basedpython spells identity as `===` / `!==`. both parse to the `CmpOp` of
# `is` / `is not`, whose surface form is instead a parametric type test, so the
# two spellings must not be collapsed into one

xs = [1]

a = xs === xs
b = xs !== xs

# the `is` spelling is a type test and stays as written
c = xs is list[int]
d = xs is not list[int]

# chained comparisons mix the spellings freely
e = xs === xs !== None is list[int] is not list[str]

# mixed with value comparisons
f = 1 === 1 == 1

# parenthesised operands
g = (xs) === (xs)
h = (xs) !== (xs)

# inside a condition
if xs === xs:
    pass

# a long chain that has to break
long_chain = (
    some_rather_long_name === another_rather_long_name
    and another_rather_long_name !== yet_another_long_name
)
```

## Output
